Audited change: e18baa25 (src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts, 12 lines added)

Scope
  The contract applies. The change adds two operator-facing refusals to the deliver path of
  src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts. The deliver command of scripts/storytime-book-pictures.ts and
  src/storytime/book-pictures.ts is the operator surface that the refusals change.

Findings
  Blocking: none.
  Nonblocking: RC-P3-1, the contract names no deliver command. Evidence and owner routing follow.

Checks of the two new refusals
  Duplicate picture-list row id (src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts:341-346). The message reads
  "The picture list holds the row <id> twice." and names the row id. The check runs after the
  approval file is read and before the first print read, before the delivered-name loop, and
  before the first write. The refusal reaches the CLI error path, which redacts the message,
  writes it to stderr, and returns 1. The command exits non-zero.

  Symlinked delivery root (src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts:348-351). The writer calls lstat on the
  delivery root. The message reads "The delivery folder <path> is a symlink; the writer refuses
  it." and names the absolute path. The check runs before the mkdir at line 488 and before the
  writes at lines 489 and 490, so a refused run creates no folder and no file.

Checks of the normal run
  A missing delivery root makes lstat return ENOENT. lstatOrNull returns null, the root check
  passes, and the writer creates the folder as before.

  The week 1 delivery folders delivery-muse-v1 and delivery-muse-v2 are real directories, so the
  root check accepts the production folders.

  A folder that holds the same manifest still works. The writer reads manifest.json, compares the
  bytes, and keeps the file when the bytes match (src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts:455-464).

  The picture list holds 196 rows with 196 distinct ids. The week 1 set holds 30 rows with 30
  distinct ids, so the new duplicate check accepts the operator run.

  The operator approval list docs/storytime/l2-unit1/w01/muse/approved.json holds 30 entries, one
  per week 1 row. It pins the picture list SHA-256 6d05dfc5..., which equals the contract pin at
  contract.md:10-11 and the measured hash of the Workbooks list file.

Checks of the delivery contract
  The fileVersion rule holds. contract.md:24-26 states that an approval entry with fileVersion N
  delivers <row id>-vN.png and <row id>-line-vN.png from one candidate at version N. The code
  keeps that rule in deliveredNames (src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts:188-204). The change e18baa25
  touches no line of that rule.

  The PM decision A holds. contract.md:28-30 states that the Workbooks stage 1 reader matches a
  manifest entry by the row id and that Workbooks owns that change. The Forge side provides the
  row id. manifestJob copies rowCaptureJob, which sets id to row.id (src/storytime/muse-delivery.ts:326-329,
  src/storytime/book-pictures.ts:3611-3629). The week 1 v2 manifest holds 30 jobs, 26 at version 1
  and 4 at version 2, with the batches w01/color and w01/lineart, and the folder holds 60 PNG
  files. The 4 fileVersion rows use the -v2 names and the other 26 rows keep the -v1 names.

Earlier findings of this role
  RCV2-1 withdrawn. The PM decision A of 2026-11-02, 03:1x ICT, assigns the stage 1 row match to
  the Workbooks reader, and the contract records that decision at contract.md:28-30. The Forge
  manifest gives every job the row id as job.id, so the finding stays closed and is not re-raised.

  RCV2-2 withdrawn. The same PM decision A sets the row scope of the stage 1 run, and the plan
  records it at plan.md:5129-5133 and plan.md:5174-5175. The Forge side takes the row set from the
  list and the week filter (src/storytime/book-pictures.ts:4743-4748), so the finding stays closed
  and is not re-raised.

  RCV2-3 withdrawn. contract.md:24-26 now states the fileVersion rule and contract.md:28-30 states
  the decision A match by row id, both added by commit 08edc06a in the phase range. The contract
  no longer drifts, so the nit stays closed.

Nonblocking finding
  RC-P3-1 [Nit] measure/tracks/asset_storytime_l2_unit1_pictures_20261025/contract.md:43-85. The
  Commands section lists plan, render, lineart-smoke, precheck-minimax, precheck-kimi, manifest,
  sheet and verify. It holds no entry for the deliver command, which the CLI accepts
  (src/storytime/book-pictures.ts:4628) and runs at lines 4726-4755 with the flags --list,
  --approvals, --muse and --delivery (src/storytime/book-pictures.ts:4637, 4729). The contract
  holds no deliver refusal rule either, so the two new refusals live only in the code and in
  plan.md:5199-5212. An operator who reads contract.md cannot learn how to run the phase delivery.
  This item differs from RCV2-3, which was about the fileVersion rule. Owner: Green.

Limits of this review
  No vitest ran. The Green log measure/runs/asset_storytime_l2_unit1_pictures_20261025/jr-green-adv-fix.log
  records 190 of 190 tests passed in five files, and a mutation proof where removing the duplicate
  row check fails ADV9.

  No browser, no render, no server, and no live deliver probe ran. The refusals and the normal
  path rest on code reading at the audited HEAD and on the week 1 delivery artifacts. The out/
  reads come from the working tree, because out/ holds build output.

  No file outside measure/runs/** changed.

